### Modify: `apps/server/src/orchestration/Layers/ProjectionPipeline.ts`

1. **Import** the new repository:
   ```typescript
   import { ConversationSearchRepository } from "../../persistence/Services/ConversationSearch.ts";
   import { ConversationSearchRepositoryLive } from "../../persistence/Layers/ConversationSearch.ts";
   ```

2. **Yield** the repository in `makeOrchestrationProjectionPipeline`:
   ```typescript
   const conversationSearchRepository = yield* ConversationSearchRepository;
   ```

3. **Add a new projector** named `"projection.conversation-search"` to the `ORCHESTRATION_PROJECTOR_NAMES` const:
   ```typescript
   export const ORCHESTRATION_PROJECTOR_NAMES = {
     // ...existing
     conversationSearch: "projection.conversation-search",
   } as const;
   ```

4. **Implement** `applyConversationSearchProjection`:
   ```typescript
   const applyConversationSearchProjection: ProjectorDefinition["apply"] = (event, _attachmentSideEffects) =>
     Effect.gen(function* () {
       switch (event.type) {
         case "thread.message-sent": {
           // Index the message text in FTS
           yield* conversationSearchRepository.indexMessage({
             threadId: event.payload.threadId,
             messageId: event.payload.messageId,
             role: event.payload.role,
             text: event.payload.text,
           });
           return;
         }

         case "thread.created": {
           // Index the initial thread title
           yield* conversationSearchRepository.updateThreadTitle({
             threadId: event.payload.threadId,
             title: event.payload.title,
           });
           return;
         }

         case "thread.meta-updated": {
           // Update thread title in FTS if title changed
           if (event.payload.title !== undefined) {
             yield* conversationSearchRepository.updateThreadTitle({
               threadId: event.payload.threadId,
               title: event.payload.title,
             });
           }
           return;
         }

         case "thread.deleted": {
           // Remove all FTS entries for this thread
           yield* conversationSearchRepository.removeThread({
             threadId: event.payload.threadId,
           });
           return;
         }

         case "thread.reverted": {
           // On revert, remove all messages for this thread from FTS
           // and re-index the retained messages
           const existingMessages = yield* projectionThreadMessageRepository.listByThreadId({
             threadId: event.payload.threadId,
           });
           // Delete all message FTS entries for this thread
           yield* sql`DELETE FROM projection_messages_fts WHERE thread_id = ${event.payload.threadId}`
             .pipe(Effect.mapError(toPersistenceSqlError("ConversationSearchProjection.revert:delete")));
           // Re-index retained messages
           yield* Effect.forEach(
             existingMessages,
             (msg) => conversationSearchRepository.indexMessage({
               threadId: msg.threadId,
               messageId: msg.messageId,
               role: msg.role,
               text: msg.text,
             }),
             { concurrency: 1 },
           );
           return;
         }

         default:
           return;
       }
     });
   ```

5. **Register** the projector in the `projectors` array:
   ```typescript
   {
     name: ORCHESTRATION_PROJECTOR_NAMES.conversationSearch,
     apply: applyConversationSearchProjection,
   },
   ```

6. **Add layer** to `OrchestrationProjectionPipelineLive`:
   ```typescript
   Layer.provideMerge(ConversationSearchRepositoryLive),
   ```

This approach keeps FTS sync inline with the projection pipeline — no SQL triggers needed. Each projector runs inside a transaction, so FTS updates are atomic with the projection state update.

Add a WS handler for the `orchestration.searchConversations` method.

### Modify: `apps/server/src/wsServer.ts`

1. **Import** the ConversationSearchRepository:
   ```typescript
   import { ConversationSearchRepository } from "./persistence/Services/ConversationSearch.ts";
   ```

2. **Yield** the repository in `createServer` (alongside existing service yields like `orchestrationEngine`, `projectionReadModelQuery`, etc.):
   ```typescript
   const conversationSearchRepository = yield* ConversationSearchRepository;
   ```

3. **Add a case** in the `routeRequest` function's switch statement, before the `default` case:
   ```typescript
   case ORCHESTRATION_WS_METHODS.searchConversations: {
     const body = stripRequestTag(request.body);
     const rows = yield* conversationSearchRepository.searchAll(body);
     // Group results by thread
     const threadMap = new Map<string, {
       threadId: string;
       threadTitle: string;
       createdAt: string;
       updatedAt: string;
       matches: Array<{ messageId?: string; snippet: string; relevance: number }>;
     }>();
     for (const row of rows) {
       let entry = threadMap.get(row.threadId);
       if (!entry) {
         entry = {
           threadId: row.threadId,
           threadTitle: row.threadTitle,
           createdAt: row.threadCreatedAt,
           updatedAt: row.threadUpdatedAt,
           matches: [],
         };
         threadMap.set(row.threadId, entry);
       }
       entry.matches.push({
         ...(row.messageId !== null ? { messageId: row.messageId } : {}),
         snippet: row.snippet,
         relevance: row.relevance,
       });
     }
     return { results: Array.from(threadMap.values()) };
   }
   ```

4. **Handle thread-reference attachments** in `normalizeDispatchCommand`: The existing code iterates over `turnStartCommand.message.attachments` and processes each one as an image (parseBase64DataUrl, write file, etc.). Now with `ThreadMentionAttachment` in the union, thread-reference attachments will also be iterated. We need to skip non-image attachments:

   In the `normalizedAttachments` forEach handler, add an early return for non-image types:
   ```typescript
   const normalizedAttachments = yield* Effect.forEach(
     turnStartCommand.message.attachments,
     (attachment) =>
       Effect.gen(function* () {
         // Pass through non-image attachments (e.g., thread-reference) as-is
         if (attachment.type !== "image") {
           return attachment as any; // ChatAttachment
         }
         // ... existing image processing code ...
       }),
     { concurrency: 1 },
   );
   ```

